PROTECTED-PATH PROTOCOL, AND WHY THERE ARE TWO COMMITS
======================================================
`tools/gatekeeper-land.sh` and `programs/ci_harness_timeout_ceiling_check.py`
are protected paths in `tools/ci/protected_landing_transition.json`. Measured
before this landing: pristine main matched the manifest's `next` state 47/47,
and its `current` state 45/47. Editing a protected path without declaring the
move first leaves the tree matching NEITHER state, and `build_receipt` parses
that manifest BEFORE it looks at any candidate — so the next landing on the
merge path would refuse for a reason that has nothing to do with it.

